DECISIONS kicom
DECISION D001 status=accepted title="HTTPS/KCL instead of direct shell"
DECISION D006 status=accepted title="Persist canonical project memory on KiCom"
DECISION D015 status=accepted title="Living Architecture separates genome, memory and phenotype"
DECISION D018 status=accepted title="No hard delete for Goal/ChatGPT memory history; archive or supersede instead"
DECISION D019 status=accepted title="Use a broad bounded Autonomy Envelope instead of per-operation admin approval"
RATIONALE D019 "Frequent low-risk approvals create human fatigue; boundaries should be defined once and enforced in code"
DECISION D020 status=accepted title="Use FreeOTP as the Human Authorization Bridge for trust-boundary crossings"
RATIONALE D020 "A short-lived human factor can authorize exact RED, production or kernel transactions directly from chat"
DECISION D021 status=accepted title="Use rolling one-time session tokens"
RATIONALE D021 "A token visible in transport logs is already spent after the request that used it"
DECISION D022 status=accepted title="Make GitHub optional only"
RATIONALE D022 "KiCom source reads, update upload, archive and primary feed must work on first-party infrastructure"
DECISION D023 status=accepted title="Treat kicomarchive as append-only release history"
RATIONALE D023 "Install/update packages, source snapshots, hashes and metadata must remain reconstructable"
DECISION D015 status=accepted title="Buffer large chat transactions inertly and rotate the main session only at commit"
RATIONALE D015 "Avoid URL and roundtrip overhead without granting fragment tokens any project-mutation authority"
DECISION D016 status=accepted title="Let exact RED approvals survive session idle for one hour"
RATIONALE D016 "A prepared binding remains hash- and state-bound; execution still requires a fresh one-use TOTP and binding revalidation"
DECISION D017 status=accepted title="Learn transaction fragment size dynamically per transport profile"
RATIONALE D017 "Successful fragments raise the remembered safe size, transport failures can back off, and idempotent retry removes ambiguity without changing authorization boundaries"
DECISION D018 status=accepted title="Use bounded past-counter grace only for normal autonomy-session opening"
RATIONALE D018 "Chat and transport latency can exceed one 30-second step; accepting the previous two counters once for session opening removes timing races while critical trust-boundary approval stays current-counter only"
DECISION D025 status=accepted title="Capability-first: separate transport capability from action authority"
RATIONALE D025 "Do not artificially cripple useful integrations or add transport barriers merely for reassurance. Prefer the simplest broad transfer path and enforce trust only when a protected action actually requires it."
DECISION D026 status=accepted title="Direct ChatGPT update is a first-class self-update transport"
RATIONALE D026 "ChatGPT can author updates inside KiCom or transfer complete ZIP packages directly without Slack, mail or GitHub; every path converges on the ordinary KiCom self-update verifier."
DECISION D027 status=accepted title="Superseded pending updates keep metadata history"
RATIONALE D027 "Replacing a pending update must not silently erase project experience; preserve superseded metadata while allowing the newer verified candidate to proceed."
DECISION D028 status=accepted title="SQLite becomes primary operational memory"
RATIONALE D028 "Transactional relational storage carries mutable state and events; Canonical KCL, Genome, secrets and immutable archives remain separate."
DECISION D029 status=accepted title="SQLite healing uses integrity checks, snapshots and rebuild mirrors"
RATIONALE D029 "A changing DB is healed by state-aware checks, quarantine, verified restore and mirror reconciliation rather than a static file hash."
DECISION D030 status=accepted title="SQLite may evolve through shadow experiments"
RATIONALE D030 "Schema and index candidates are measured and integrity-checked on a shadow copy before transactional promotion with snapshots."
DECISION D031 status=accepted title="Separate technical risk classification from authority boundary"
RATIONALE D031 "Risk drives verification depth; authority determines whether a human authorization is required."
DECISION D032 status=accepted title="Make DEV a trusted genome-covered module set"
RATIONALE D032 "Loose DEV PHP was removed by the immune guardian; trusted modules preserve integrity while keeping DEV incapable of production authority."
DECISION D033 status=accepted title="Use WebAuthn passkey for routine DEV entry"
RATIONALE D033 "Routine development should not require repeated FreeOTP codes; DEV credentials remain strictly scope-limited."
DECISION D034 status=accepted title="Harden SQLite migration, backup, import and evolution semantics"
RATIONALE D034 "Persistent operational memory needs checksum verification, actual-insert accounting, verified backup fallback and snapshot-gated promotion."
DECISION D035 status=accepted title="Preserve Slack, Mail and Opera as redundant non-authoritative paths"
RATIONALE D035 "Transport diversity improves resilience without letting any transport grant authority."
END_DECISIONS kicom
